1. Frontend cleanup — six targeted reductions across the web-ui frontend
    [x] 'content/web-ui/frontend/keyboard-bar.js': Replace scrollKeyMap with a module-scope SCROLL_KEYS Set
        - Replace the object with Set(['ArrowUp','ArrowDown','PageUp','PageDown']); change scrollKeyMap[event.key] !== undefined to SCROLL_KEYS.has(event.key)
        - The -40/40 arrow values are re-hardcoded downstream and 'pageUp'/'pageDown' are never referenced, so nothing is lost
    [x] 'content/web-ui/frontend/api-client.js': Collapse renderPrompt onto #post
        - Body becomes this.#post('/api/render-prompt', { headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' }, body: JSON.stringify({ domain, prompt }) })
        - renderPrompt duplicates #post's fetch + response.ok + error-message logic; leave boot (GET) alone
    [x] 'content/web-ui/frontend/message.js': Inline updateContent
        - At the single call site in clanker-app, replace assistantMsg.updateContent(...) with assistantMsg.content = prevContent + fullText
        - Remove the one-line updateContent method
    [x] 'content/web-ui/frontend/clanker-app.js': Drop the always-true guard ⚠️ revision
        - Remove only the if (!prevContent) conditional; keep assistantMsg.sentChars = totalChars;
        - Add a one-line comment that it seeds the chars-per-prefill-token ratio (consumed by message.js onPrefill for the live token estimates)
        - Dropping the assignment would silently degrade running stats from token-based to char-based
    [x] 'content/web-ui/frontend/messages-box.js': Dedupe setScrollLocked(false)
        - Bind one handler to both focusin and wheel instead of two identical one-liners (#handleFocusIn/#handleWheel)
    [x] 'content/web-ui/frontend/base-component.js' (+ 'content/web-ui/frontend/message.js'): Drop cosmetic comments
        - Remove //All components inherit BaseComponent...
        - Remove the // --- Prefill/Reasoning/Content segment --- markers in message.js #buildStatsLine
        - Keep the // null | 'prefill' | ... phase spec and // Surface a single prompt_progress tick.

1. Ingestion parser: enforce new closing-tag format (no path in close)
    [x] 'content/backend/asset_ingestion/ingestion_parser.py': No logic change required
        - `_close_re` already uses `FILESET_OPEN_END_TAG_BR` (`>`), so expected close is `</create>` / `</update>` — no path in closing tag
        - Confirmed by live testing: parser accepted that format once backend was restarted
    [x] 'content/a_lib/shared-assets/prompt-fragments/output-instructions/code-generation.output-template': Closing bookend examples drop path from close tag
        - `§ufsbl§` → `§fsoetbr§` (i.e. `</update>`)
        - `§cfsbl§` → `§fsoetbr§` (i.e. `</create>`)
        - Delete tags unaffected (self-closing, no separate close)

n. Delims: replace path-bearing tag constants with verb-injected f-string methods and §verb, op, args§ token format
    [x] 'content/backend/core/core/entities.py': Rewrite Delims as template + static-method source
        - Remove all path-bearing tuple constants: CREATE_FILESET_UL, UPDATE_FILESET_UL, DELETE_FILESET_UL, READ_FILESET_UL, CREATE_FILESET_BL, UPDATE_FILESET_BL, FILESET_OPEN_END_TAG, FILESET_OPEN_END_TAG_BR, FILESET_CLOSED_END_TAG, FILE_META_UL, FILE_META_CLOSE
        - Add four private format-string templates (class-level, not per-verb):
            - _OPEN_TMPL = '<{verb} path="{path}">'
            - _CLOSE_TMPL = '</{verb}>'
            - _SELF_CLOSE_TMPL = '<{verb} path="{path}"/>'
            - _SELF_CLOSE_LOC_TMPL = '<{verb} path="{path}" loc={loc}/>'
        - Add three public static methods that inject the verb before returning:
            - open(verb, path) → _OPEN_TMPL.format(verb=verb, path=path)
            - close(verb) → _CLOSE_TMPL.format(verb=verb)
            - self_close(verb, path, loc=None) → _SELF_CLOSE_TMPL or _SELF_CLOSE_LOC_TMPL depending on loc
        - Add four static prefix/suffix methods for parser regex construction:
            - open_prefix(verb) → '<{verb} path="' (format, no path)
            - open_suffix(verb) → '">'
            - self_close_prefix(verb) → '<{verb} path="'
            - self_close_suffix(verb) → '"/>'
        - Keep FILELIST_START_OPEN, FILELIST_START_CLOSE, FILELIST_END_OPEN, FILELIST_END_CLOSE, PROMPT_OPEN, PROMPT_CLOSE, MANIFEST_MEMBER as plain string constants, unchanged
        - Prohibition: no consumer outside Delims may construct a full tag by concatenating raw string fragments
    [x] 'content/backend/render_pipeline/render_service.py': Align rendering to verb static methods
        - _format_full_file: replace Delims.READ_FILESET_UL[1] + path + Delims.FILESET_OPEN_END_TAG[1] with Delims.open("file", path); replace Delims.READ_FILESET_BL[1] + path + Delims.FILESET_OPEN_END_TAG[1] with Delims.close("file")
        - _res_repo_content meta block: replace FILE_META_UL[1] + p + " loc=" + str(line_count) + FILE_META_CLOSE[1] with Delims.self_close("file_meta", p, loc=line_count)
        - _res_multi_doc: FILELIST constants for name bookends remain unchanged (no path in those tags)
        - Prohibition: no f-string in render_service may hardcode "<file", "</file", "<create", or any other verb-literal tag fragment
    [x] 'content/backend/render_pipeline/content_shaper.py': Rewrite _substitute_placeholders to parse §verb, op, args§ tokens
        - Remove iteration over Delims.__dict__.values() for tuple-based token→display substitution
        - Introduce a regex to match the new token format: §<verb>, <op>[, <arg1>[, <arg2>]]§
        - Resolve each match by exact string equality on the verb field, then dispatch on op:
            - "open" → Delims.open(verb, args[0])
            - "close" → Delims.close(verb)
            - "selfclose" → Delims.self_close(verb, args[0], loc=int(args[1]) if len(args) > 1 else None)
        - Unknown verb or op: leave token in place (pass-through), do not raise
        - Prohibition: the shaper must not contain any hardcoded "<create path=\" or similar display-string literal
    [x] 'content/backend/asset_ingestion/ingestion_parser.py': Build regex patterns from Delims prefix/suffix methods
        - _open_re: build by iterating the verb set, composing re.escape(Delims.open_prefix(verb)) + named-capture-group + re.escape(Delims.open_suffix(verb)) for open-verb tags, and re.escape(Delims.self_close_prefix(verb)) + named-capture-group + re.escape(Delims.self_close_suffix(verb)) for self-close-verb tags (delete)
        - _close_re: build by iterating the verb set, composing re.escape(Delims.close(verb)) for each verb that has a close tag (create, update)
        - Remove the inline re.escape(Delims.X[1]) construction; all pattern fragments derive from Delims static methods
        - Prohibition: no regex fragment may be hand-escaped at the parser call-site outside of re.escape(Delims.method(...))
    [x] 'content/a_lib/shared-assets/prompt-fragments/output-instructions/code-generation.output-template': Migrate token format to §verb, op, args§
        - Replace all old tokens (§cfsul§, §fsoet§, §cfsbl§, §fsoetbr§, §ufsul§, §ufsbl§, §dfsul§, §fscet§) with the new format:
            - §create, open, path3§ / §create, close§ (replaces old create open/close)
            - §update, open, path1§ / §update, close§ (replaces old update open/close)
            - §delete, selfclose, path5§ (replaces old delete self-closing)
        - Expected display output after shaper substitution is identical to before
        - Prohibition: no old-style §cfsul§, §rfsul§, §fsoet§ etc. token may remain in the file
    [x] 'content/test/ingestion/code_ingestion_parser_tests.py': Switch helper constructors to Delims static methods
        - _create_open(path): replace Delims tuple-concatenation with e.Delims.open("create", path)
        - _create_close(): replace with e.Delims.close("create")
        - _update_open(path): replace with e.Delims.open("update", path)
        - _update_close(): replace with e.Delims.close("update")
        - _delete_tag(path): replace with e.Delims.self_close("delete", path)
        - All test assertions remain unchanged (same expected display strings)
        - Prohibition: no test may reference a removed Delims constant
    [x] 'content/test/ingestion/code_ingestion_service_tests.py': Switch helper constructors to Delims static methods
        - Same five helper-function replacements as parser tests
        - Prohibition: no test may reference a removed Delims constant
    [x] 'content/test/render/render_contentshaper_tests.py': Update input tokens to §verb, op, args§ format
        - test_template_file_placeholder_substitution: input tokens change from §llul§ path §llur§ style to §file, open, path§ / §file, close§ (note: llul/llur are FILELIST, not fileset — verify these remain unchanged or get their own token treatment)
        - test_template_file_fileset_placeholder_substitution: input changes from §cfsul§src/new.py§fsoet§ / §cfsbl§§fsoetbr§ etc. to §create, open, src/new.py§ / §create, close§ / §delete, selfclose, src/old.py§
        - test_template_file_no_placeholder_tokens_remain: input tokens updated to new format; assertion (no § in result) stays the same
        - test_truncation_applies_after_substitution, test_from_line_on_template, test_up_to_on_template: if they use old § tokens in input, update to new format
        - Prohibition: no test may hardcode an old-style token (§cfsul§ etc.) as input

